      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The afflicted Colorado Avalanche, reeling from a devastating loss of key personnel when injured stars Cale Makar and Nathan MacKinnon were sidelined, saw their playoff hopes end in a final decisive elimination. This came after the team faced a mid-season leadership change, a moment of instability and disruption that a stabilizing leader, John Tortorella, stepped into to provide steadying leadership through hardship. Ultimately, the series conclusion was a sweep by the victorious organization, advancing at another's expense to the championship series qualification.",
